{"type": "survey_submit", "survey_type": "post", "puzzle_idx": null, "answers": {"puzzle_1_rate_again": 3, "puzzle_1_guesses": "never", "puzzle_2_rate_again": 4, "puzzle_2_guesses": "never", "puzzle_3_rate_again": 2, "puzzle_3_guesses": "never", "puzzle_3_rating_reason": "The borders were all straight forward, which gave a good basis to start. The deductions that followed were straight forward too.", "puzzle_2_rating_reason": "I was stumped more often than on puzzle one. There were more smaller numbers, sometimes I need to take more time to find the next move.", "strategy": "I glance the grid to search for large numbers or a row with many numbers, those are easy start with, because you can find overlaps in the possible positions. I also try to start with the borders because having only one possible location to extend to makes the deductions easy.", "puzzle_1_rating_reason": "There were some large numbers, it was easy enough to start and it didn't feel difficult to complete.", "comments": "The easiest puzzles would have rows of 10's, 9's or 8's, the numbers in these puzzles are generally smaller so they weren't super easy. The grid size is small though so the puzzles aren't very difficult. A larger grid size would have more variation in possible patterns."}, "t": "2026-03-10T16:26:51.903100+00:00"}
